glossary_text='''Agent|Agente|A system that selects actions from observations or internal state.|1
Actuator|Actuador|A mechanism through which an agent changes its environment.|1
Percept|Percepción|An observation available to the agent at a particular time.|1
Rationality|Racionalidad|Choosing actions that maximise expected performance given available information.|1
PEAS|Rendimiento, entorno, actuadores y sensores|A framework for specifying an agent task.|1
Partial observability|Observabilidad parcial|The observation does not reveal all decision-relevant state.|1
State space|Espacio de estados|The states and transitions admitted by a problem model.|2
Frontier|Frontera|Discovered search nodes waiting to be expanded.|2
Path cost|Coste del camino|The sum of action costs along a path.|2
Completeness|Completitud|A guarantee of finding a solution when one exists under stated assumptions.|2
Optimality|Optimalidad|A guarantee of returning a solution with minimum cost under stated assumptions.|2
Cutoff|Interrupción por límite|A search stopped by a resource limit; not proof of unsolvability.|2
Heuristic|Heurística|An estimate used to guide a search decision.|3
Admissibility|Admisibilidad|A heuristic never overestimates the optimal remaining cost.|3
Consistency|Consistencia|For every edge, h(n) is at most its cost plus h(n′).|3
Reopening|Reapertura|Expanding a state again after discovering a better path to it.|3
Dominance|Dominancia|One admissible heuristic is at least as large as another at every state.|3
Tie-breaking|Desempate|A specified rule for choosing among equal-priority candidates.|3
Domain|Dominio|The current candidate values for a CSP variable.|4
Constraint|Restricción|A condition that valid assignments must satisfy.|4
Arc consistency|Consistencia de arco|Every remaining value has support in the neighbouring variable on that arc.|4
Forward checking|Comprobación hacia delante|Removing incompatible values from unassigned neighbours after an assignment.|4
MRV|Mínimos valores restantes|Choose an unassigned variable with the smallest current domain.|4
Global constraint|Restricción global|A constraint involving a collection of variables, such as AllDifferent.|4
Minimax|Minimax|Choose against an optimal opponent in a zero-sum decision model.|5
Alpha–beta pruning|Poda alfa–beta|Skip branches that cannot change the minimax root decision.|5
Evaluation function|Función de evaluación|An estimate of position quality at a search cutoff.|5
Expectimax|Expectimax|Back up expected utility at chance nodes and choices at decision nodes.|5
Utility|Utilidad|The numerical preference measure used by the decision model.|5
Move ordering|Ordenación de movimientos|The order in which successor actions are considered.|5
MDP|Proceso de decisión de Markov|A model of states, actions, transitions, rewards and an objective.|6
Return|Retorno|The accumulated, possibly discounted, future reward.|6
Discount factor|Factor de descuento|The weight gamma applied per future time step.|6
Bellman backup|Actualización de Bellman|A value update using immediate reward and successor values.|6
Temporal difference|Diferencia temporal|Learning from a sampled reward and a bootstrapped value estimate.|6
Q-learning|Q-learning|An off-policy update that uses the largest next-action value.|6
SARSA|SARSA|An on-policy update using the next action actually selected.|6
Exploration|Exploración|Taking actions to obtain information rather than only exploiting current estimates.|6
Termination|Terminación|The task reaches a genuine terminal state.|6
Truncation|Truncamiento|An external limit stops interaction without necessarily terminating the underlying task.|6'''
glossary=[dict(en=a,es=b,definition=c,unit=int(d)) for a,b,c,d in (line.split('|') for line in glossary_text.splitlines())]
weeks=[(1,'Agents: task and environment',1,'Specify PEAS and environment assumptions.','Compare reflex and model-based behaviour.','Vacuum laboratory and foundation challenge.'),(2,'Agents: modelling and evidence',1,'Rationality and expected utility.','Coupled Loopover actions and invariant reasoning.','Agent policy exercise and applied challenge.'),(3,'Search: formalise and trace',2,'States, actions, goals and path costs.','BFS, DFS and duplicate detection.','Trace shared instances and report frontier contents.'),(4,'Search: costs and limits',2,'UCS and goal-test timing.','Depth limits, cutoffs and resource growth.','Implement UCS; replay returned paths.'),(5,'Heuristics: justify the estimate',3,'Greedy search and A*.','Admissibility, consistency and counterexamples.','Heuristic audit and foundation challenge.'),(6,'Heuristics: implement and compare',3,'Reopening and stale entries.','Loopover lower bounds and experimental design.','Implement A*; compare with a certified shallow baseline.'),(7,'Constraints: model and propagate',4,'Variables, domains and constraints.','Forward checking and arc consistency.','Colouring laboratory and local-versus-global reasoning.'),(8,'Constraints: search efficiently',4,'MRV and value ordering.','Global constraints and local search.','Implement colouring; compare propagation strategies.'),(9,'Games: reason against an opponent',5,'Minimax assumptions and utility.','Alpha–beta exact values and bounds.','Trace pruning and implement stable tie handling.'),(10,'Games: evaluate and order',5,'Cutoff evaluation and move ordering.','Chance nodes and expectimax.','Compare leaf evaluations on the same tree.'),(11,'RL: model sequential rewards',6,'MDPs, returns and discounting.','Bellman backups and value iteration.','Calculate targets and inspect value propagation.'),(12,'RL: learn from samples',6,'TD, Q-learning and SARSA.','Exploration and terminal versus truncated episodes.','Run the Python exercise and multi-seed comparisons.'),(13,'RL: evaluate and diagnose',6,'Frozen-policy evaluation and dispersion.','Reward design and generalisation.','Complete the applied/extension RL challenge.'),(14,'Project clinic',3,'Audit Loopover models and optimality claims.','Reproduce another team’s experiment.','Peer review with the project rubric.'),(15,'Synthesis and defence',6,'Connect assumptions across the six models.','Explain a failure case and defend a design choice.','Project demonstration, targeted review and reflection.')]
challenges=[dict(id=f'u{i+1}-{level}',unit=i+1,level=level,title=t,prompt=p,evidence=e,minutes=[20,45,75][j],hints=hints[i],rubric=rubric) for i,unit in enumerate(briefs) for j,(level,(t,p,e)) in enumerate(zip(['foundation','applied','extension'],unit))]
